## Still open

- The two Java lexer helper files carry no license notice. This needs resolving before any redistribution.
- cljstyle needs to be run by someone with permission.
- A number-to-string primitive in `data` would allow guest-visible `str()` and error messages that include counts. That is an owner or Architect call.
- Remaining differences from Python:
  - integer overflow past 64 bits is a host error on the JVM;
  - `isinstance` works only on class instances;
  - dict `==` compares identity;
  - float text outside roughly 1e-4 to 1e16 differs from Python on the JVM;
  - each compiled unit carries its own copy of the prelude.
- Heap growth, since cells are never reclaimed: one flag cell per `call-ec` or `try` activation, and one cell per function object.

As the brief required, safepoints and guest-visible line numbers were not added to the lowering.

